intensely interesting,

2102
01:14:55,975 --> 01:14:57,368
and affordable toys

2103
01:14:57,368 --> 01:14:59,967
that are safe, soft, and colorful.

2104
01:14:59,967 --> 01:15:00,800
Goodnight.

2105
01:15:00,800 --> 01:15:02,348
- And may God bless.

2106
01:15:02,348 --> 01:15:04,931
(upbeat music)

2107
01:15:08,913 --> 01:15:09,996
- Mike, look!

2108
01:15:09,996 --> 01:15:11,652
- Oh, we're coming out
of the game thing then.

2109
01:15:11,652 --> 01:15:12,485
- That was neat.

2110
01:15:12,485 --> 01:15:14,365
- Certainly was a neat game thing we did.

2111
01:15:14,365 --> 01:15:15,939
Oh boy.

2112
01:15:15,939 --> 01:15:17,687
- I tell you there have
been people through here.

2113
01:15:17,687 --> 01:15:19,435
- Jack Weston!

2114
01:15:19,435 --> 01:15:20,539
Or George.

2115
01:15:20,539 --> 01:15:23,198
- George Weston, lost?

2116
01:15:23,198 --> 01:15:24,031
- Hello?

2117
01:15:24,031 --> 01:15:24,864
I'm George Weston.

2118
01:15:24,864 --> 01:15:25,931
- 1902.

2119
01:15:25,931 --> 01:15:26,764
- Mike!

2120
01:15:26,764 --> 01:15:27,847
- Ugh, grody.

2121
01:15:30,282 --> 01:15:33,478
- He must have starved to death.

2122
01:15:33,478 --> 01:15:36,388
I'm getting awfully worried, Mike.

2123
01:15:36,388 --> 01:15:38,366
- Me too, Carol.

2124
01:15:38,366 --> 01:15:40,088
- Why did I ever have
to bring you down here?

2125
01:15:40,088 --> 01:15:40,963
Go, Mike.

2126
01:15:40,963 --> 01:15:43,070
- All you do is bring me down, babe.

2127
01:15:43,070 --> 01:15:45,266
- Don't let her bring you down.
It's only castles burning.

2128
01:15:45,266 --> 01:15:47,232
- What do you suppose
your mother's thinking?

2129
01:15:47,232 --> 01:15:48,277
- Well, they wouldn't tell her.

2130
01:15:48,277 --> 01:15:50,430
She's in the hospital having a baby.

2131
01:15:50,430 --> 01:15:51,396
- And what about your dad?

2132
01:15:51,396 --> 01:15:53,613
- Dad? We're still trying
to find out who he is.

2133
01:15:53,613 --> 01:15:56,430
- I think he can take it.

2134
01:15:56,430 --> 01:15:57,930
- My mother can't.

2135
01:15:59,744 --> 01:16:01,516
Not after what happened to my father.

2136
01:16:01,516 --> 01:16:03,737
- Don't make yourself feel bad, Carol.

2137
01:16:03,737 --> 01:16:05,737
- I can do that for you.

2138
01:16:09,051 --> 01:16:11,718
- Don't you worry about it then.

2139
01:16:13,512 --> 01:16:16,077
- All of a sudden I feel hungry.

2140
01:16:16,077 --> 01:16:17,687
- Me too.
- Not for spider.

2141
01:16:17,687 --> 01:16:19,547
- I just remembered I've
got a candy bar with me.

2142
01:16:19,547 --> 01:16:21,964
- What are you going to have?

2143
01:16:24,691 --> 01:16:26,274
- It's a Clark Bar.

2144
01:16:27,129 --> 01:16:29,221
- Ugh, must have gotten
warm in your pocket.

2145
01:16:29,221 --> 01:16:33,983
It is good food, however.
(eerie screeching)

2146
01:16:33,983 --> 01:16:37,233
- Hey, did you just make a yummy noise?

2147
01:16:41,628 --> 01:16:43,251
- No, this always happens at dinner.

2148
01:16:43,251 --> 01:16:47,084
Have your little friend
go home now, will you?

2149
01:16:47,953 --> 01:16:50,713
- Convoy with Kris
Kristofferson and Ali MacGraw.

2150
01:16:50,713 --> 01:16:53,440
Up next is Kenny Rogers in Six Pack.

2151
01:16:53,440 --> 01:16:54,462
- Good movie.

2152
01:16:54,462 --> 01:16:57,373
♪ We are the men of Texico ♪

2153
01:16:57,373 --> 01:16:59,623
♪ The star ♪

2154
01:17:04,237 --> 01:17:05,619
- All right, you men, make it snappy.

2155
01:17:05,619 --> 01:17:07,609
Let's get that gear off that truck.

2156
01:17:07,609 --> 01:17:10,749
- Break out the little cocktail weenies.

2157
01:17:10,749 --> 01:17:11,783
- I'll just stay out here

2158
01:17:11,783 --> 01:17:15,283
and bark out belligerent fat-assed orders.

2159
01:17:16,417 --> 01:17:18,073
- Good, good, keep it coming.

2160
01:17:18,073 --> 01:17:19,490
Come on, come on.

2161
01:17:21,961 --> 01:17:23,695
Come on, oh, come on, Pops.

2162
01:17:23,695 --> 01:17:24,825
Is that all you can carry?

2163
01:17:24,825 --> 01:17:26,895
Take two next time.

2164
01:17:26,895 --> 01:17:27,825
- Yeah, case of Shabbos.

2165
01:17:27,825 --> 01:17:29,103
Good boy, good boy.

2166
01:17:29,103 --> 01:17:31,977
- Carol always lets me know
when she isn't coming home.

2167
01:17:31,977 --> 01:17:33,909
Always, but today.

2168
01:17:33,909 --> 01:17:34,742
I don't know.

2169
01:17:34,742 --> 01:17:36,517
She just wasn't herself.

2170
01:17:36,517 --> 01:17:39,586
She attached too much
importance to that bracelet.

2171
01:17:39,586 --> 01:17:42,247
Oh, I hope she and Mike haven't
gone back into that cave.

2172
01:17:42,247 --> 01:17:43,830
- Shut up, shut up!

2173
01:17:46,859 --> 01:17:47,692
- Carol, do you see?

2174
01:17:47,692 --> 01:17:49,536
This is the place where we got lost.

2175
01:17:49,536 --> 01:17:51,156
Oh, I know the way is through there.

2176
01:17:51,156 --> 01:17:52,769
- But the spider, Mike.

2177
01:17:52,769 --> 01:17:53,689
- We stay here, it will find us.

2178
01:17:53,689 --> 01:17:54,725
Come on, let's run for it.

2179
01:17:54,725 --> 01:17:56,035
- Let's find this place where we're safe

2180
01:17:56,035 --> 01:17:58,285
from these processed shots.

2181
01:18:01,462 --> 01:18:02,303
- There's the hole we fell through.

2182
01:18:02,303 --> 01:18:03,947
We haven't got far to go now.

2183
01:18:03,947 --> 01:18:06,372
I'll climb through the web.

2184
01:18:06,372 --> 01:18:09,867
- Hey, I saw this in Beastmaster
about 60 times on cable.

2185
01:18:09,867 --> 01:18:11,169
- Right after Roadhouse.

2186
01:18:11,169 --> 01:18:12,336
- Good movies.

2187
01:18:16,897 --> 01:18:17,730
- I'm stuck!

2188
01:18:17,730 --> 01:18:18,599
- Give me your hand.

2189
01:18:18,599 --> 01:18:19,432
Give me your hand.

2190
01:18:19,432 --> 01:18:21,265
- Hey, Moe, I'm stuck.

2191
01:18:23,061 --> 01:18:25,085
(eerie screeching)

2192
01:18:25,085 --> 01:18:26,073
- It's coming!

2193
01:18:26,073 --> 01:18:27,879
- It sounds like my
grandma in the morning.

2194
01:18:27,879 --> 01:18:29,225
- Let's get that extra
dynamite out of here.

2195
01:18:29,225 --> 01:18:30,058
- Ex-try?

2196
01:18:33,617 --> 01:18:35,343
- Well, that'll be the
end of our spider's night,

2197
01:18:35,343 --> 01:18:36,582
eh Kingman?

2198
01:18:36,582 --> 01:18:37,513
(chuckling)

2199
01:18:37,513 --> 01:18:39,550
- Maybe, but you said last time.

2200
01:18:39,550 --> 01:18:41,103
- Now this time it's for sure.

2201
01:18:41,103 --> 01:18:42,151
It's got to die.

2202
01:18:42,151 --> 01:18:43,611
No living organism can survive for long

2203
01:18:43,611 --> 01:18:45,795
once its food supply is cut off.

2204
01:18:45,795 --> 01:18:47,865
- We'll be ready to blow her
up in a couple of seconds.

2205
01:18:47,865 --> 01:18:49,349
- Let her blow when you're ready.

2206
01:18:49,349 --> 01:18:53,259
- Well, surely they'll see
our car at the entrance.

2207
01:18:53,259 --> 01:18:54,467
- I don't think so.

2208
01:18:54,467 --> 01:18:55,811
- Get back, all you men.

2209
01:18:55,811 --> 01:18:56,916
I don't want anyone hurt.

2210
01:18:56,916 --> 01:18:58,882
- Except for the kids in the cave.

2211
01:18:58,882 --> 01:19:00,432
(chuckling)

2212
01:19:00,432 --> 01:19:01,432
I can't see.

2213
01:19:05,219 --> 01:19:07,865
- Can't you carry more than a hammer?

2214
01:19:07,865 --> 01:19:10,441
(tense music)

2215
01:19:10,441 --> 01:19:11,671
- Then when Carol was three-

2216
01:19:11,671 --> 01:19:14,753
- Shut up, would you shut up?

2217
01:19:14,753 --> 01:19:16,593
- Isn't that Joe's car over there?

2218
01:19:16,593 --> 01:19:17,777
- Yes, it is.

2219
01:19:17,777 --> 01:19:18,694
- Why, yes.

2220
01:19:23,631 --> 01:19:24,965
- It's my car now!

2221
01:19:24,965 --> 01:19:26,594
(cackling)

2222
01:19:26,594 --> 01:19:28,243
(screaming)

2223
01:19:28,243 --> 01:19:31,326
(explosion rumbling)

2224
01:19:33,387 --> 01:19:37,225
- Oops, sorry kids.
- It's a trampoline.

2225
01:19:37,225 --> 01:19:39,595
- You know, just dawns on me.

2226
01:19:39,595 --> 01:19:40,872
I wonder if anyone is in that cave?

2227
01:19:40,872 --> 01:19:41,861
Maybe we should have checked.

2228
01:19:41,861 --> 01:19:42,873
- You sealed them up.

2229
01:19:42,873 --> 01:19:45,253
You're going to have to open
that cave and get them out.

2230
01:19:45,253 --> 01:19:46,348
- Now don't get excited.

2231
01:19:46,348 --> 01:19:48,694
We're going to do
everything for them we can.

2232
01:19:48,694 --> 01:19:50,522
How do we go about it, Haskell?

2233
01:19:50,522 --> 01:19:51,994
- Open up the cave again?

2234
01:19:51,994 --> 01:19:53,660
- Hmm.
- That's easy to say, Sheriff,

2235
01:19:53,660 --> 01:19:55,628
but it's going to take some doing.

2236
01:19:55,628 --> 01:19:58,250
Well we blew up tons of earth
and rock over that opening.

2237
01:19:58,250 --> 01:20:00,202
Brought half a hillside down.

2238
01:20:00,202 --> 01:20:02,210
- This guy must be Bert
Gordon's nephew or something.

2239
01:20:02,210 --> 01:20:03,269
- We better start clearing it away.

2240
01:20:03,269 --> 01:20:04,507
- It'll take days or maybe a week.

2241
01:20:04,507 --> 01:20:05,634
- There isn't that much time.

2242
01:20:05,634 --> 01:20:06,579
If the spider doesn't get them,

2243
01:20:06,579 --> 01:20:08,314
the bad air will.

2244
01:20:08,314 --> 01:20:09,431
- Well then we better get going,

2245
01:20:09,431 --> 01:20:11,086
the sooner, the better.

2246
01:20:11,086 --> 01:20:12,166
You've got a car.

2247
01:20:12,166 --> 01:20:14,178
Go into town and get them
to send out a bulldozer.

2248
01:20:14,178 --> 01:20:16,456
- And some sandwiches, whoever you are.

2249
01:20:16,456 --> 01:20:17,343
- See that flat shelf,

2250
01:20:17,343 --> 01:20:18,698
a little higher up the mountain?

2251
01:20:18,698 --> 01:20:22,550
Suppose we dug straight down from there?

2252
01:20:22,550 --> 01:20:24,224
- How about it, Haskell?

2253
01:20:24,224 --> 01:20:25,656
- Looks good to me.

2254
01:20:25,656 --> 01:20:28,153
Let's get those ropes, picks,
and shovels out of that truck.

2255
01:20:28,153 --> 01:20:30,094
Here's where we going to work.

2256
01:20:30,094 --> 01:20:30,927
- Who is that guy?

2257
01:20:30,927 --> 01:20:33,260
He's stinks like mummy meat.

2258
01:20:35,074 --> 01:20:36,801
- First they want us to close the cave,

2259
01:20:36,801 --> 01:20:40,098
then they want us to open the cave.

2260
01:20:40,098 --> 01:20:42,204
- What's your problem?

2261
01:20:42,204 --> 01:20:44,906
- You don't want to look at
it like that, Mrs. Flynn.

2262
01:20:44,906 --> 01:20:47,402
You've got to remember
that cave is a big place

2263
01:20:47,402 --> 01:20:49,221
and those kids have a lot of sense.

2264
01:20:49,221 --> 01:20:51,760
They'll find places where
the spider can't get at them.

2265
01:20:51,760 --> 01:20:53,140
- If we can dig our way in,

2266
01:20:53,140 --> 01:20:54,888
what's to keep it from getting at us?

2267
01:20:54,888 --> 01:20:55,801
- I don't know.

2268
01:20:55,801 --> 01:20:57,641
What do you say, Kingman?

2269
01:20:57,641 --> 01:20:59,618
- We got to have some kind
of an effective weapon.

2270
01:20:59,618 --> 01:21:02,379
I guess that that's obvious.

2271
01:21:02,379 --> 01:21:04,240
That power line across the hills.

2272
01:21:04,240 --> 01:21:05,073
- Which one?

2273
01:21:05,073 --> 01:21:05,906
Oh, that one?

2274
01:21:05,906 --> 01:21:06,739
- We could bring a cable over from there.

2275
01:21:06,739 --> 01:21:07,656
- What for?

2276
01:21:09,276 --> 01:21:10,852
- Get better reception.
- Electrocute the beast.

2277
01:21:10,852 --> 01:21:13,352
(tense music)

2278
01:21:15,016 --> 01:21:16,777
- Big, sweaty men working long hours

2279
01:21:16,777 --> 01:21:17,993
to get the job done,

2280
01:21:17,993 --> 01:21:19,708
desperately in need of Aqua Velva.

2281
01:21:19,708 --> 01:21:21,397
- Quarter mile of insulated copper cable

2282
01:21:21,397 --> 01:21:22,962
this side of Springdale.

2283
01:21:22,962 --> 01:21:23,907
- Check in my trunk.

2284
01:21:23,907 --> 01:21:27,964
- Seems to me I saw a lot
of that stuff in there.

2285
01:21:27,964 --> 01:21:29,598
- Do you want to go for
it in the truck, Simpson?

2286
01:21:29,598 --> 01:21:30,782
- Yeah.
- Kinky.

2287
01:21:30,782 --> 01:21:33,449
- Go for it in the truck.
- What?

2288
01:21:34,905 --> 01:21:36,109
- How's it coming?

2289
01:21:36,109 --> 01:21:39,109
- Not bad, but we have plenty to go.

2290
01:21:40,099 --> 01:21:42,305
- Stay off the moon.

2291
01:21:42,305 --> 01:21:44,410
(imitating wind whistling)

2292
01:21:44,410 --> 01:21:46,077
- Oh, hey, what the?

2293
01:21:50,574 --> 01:21:54,521
- Hey, did the earth move for you, honey?

2294
01:21:54,521 --> 01:21:55,771
That was great.

2295
01:22:00,464 --> 01:22:02,249
- Feeling a little rocky this morning.

2296
01:22:02,249 --> 01:22:04,999
- I really got stoned last night.

2297
01:22:06,825 --> 01:22:07,658
- Carol!

2298
01:22:10,367 --> 01:22:11,200
Carol!

2299
01:22:14,105 --> 01:22:15,405
Carol!

2300
01:22:15,405 --> 01:22:17,238
- Oh, I feel so dirty.

2301
01:22:18,417 --> 01:22:19,705
- Where is it?

2302
01:22:19,705 --> 01:22:22,741
- Looks like the Wall
concert got out of hand.

2303
01:22:22,741 --> 01:22:23,574
- Let's go.

2304
01:22:23,574 --> 01:22:24,407
Can you make it?

2305
01:22:24,407 --> 01:22:26,074
- I'll be all right.

2306
01:22:27,537 --> 01:22:29,113
- Wait, you got your bracelet?

2307
01:22:29,113 --> 01:22:31,137
- Would you forget that darn bracelet.

2308
01:22:31,137 --> 01:22:32,517
- But I need my bracelet.

2309
01:22:32,517 --> 01:22:34,017
- Oh, fine.
- Wait!

2310
01:22:35,424 --> 01:22:38,007
(upbeat music)

2311
01:22:43,465 --> 01:22:45,673
- Yeah, I got this
dynamite from the coyote.

2312
01:22:45,673 --> 01:22:48,590
Hope it doesn't roll back up on me.

2313
01:22:52,975 --> 01:22:55,308
(whistling)

2314
01:22:58,437 --> 01:23:01,046
- Now watch the old walrus move now.

2315
01:23:01,046 --> 01:23:03,296
(laughing)

2316
01:23:04,899 --> 01:23:05,968
- Is this the place we came in?

2317
01:23:05,968 --> 01:23:07,120
- I'm sure it was!

2318
01:23:07,120 --> 01:23:08,201
- Not anymore.

2319
01:23:08,201 --> 01:23:09,546
- They blew up the opening.

2320
01:23:09,546 --> 01:23:11,294
- What do we do?

2321
01:23:11,294 --> 01:23:12,858
- Panic?

2322
01:23:12,858 --> 01:23:14,735
(rumbling)

2323
01:23:14,735 --> 01:23:15,838
- What was that?

2324
01:23:15,838 --> 01:23:17,633
- Oh, some blasted thing.

2325
01:23:17,633 --> 01:23:20,465
- It sounds like blasting. I
bet they know we're in here.

2326
01:23:20,465 --> 01:23:22,049
I bet they're trying to get us out!

2327
01:23:22,049 --> 01:23:23,141
Help!

2328
01:23:23,141 --> 01:23:24,312
- [Both] Help!

2329
01:23:24,312 --> 01:23:25,223
- Help!

2330
01:23:25,223 --> 01:23:26,056
- Help!

2331
01:23:26,056 --> 01:23:26,889
- Help!

2332
01:23:27,912 --> 01:23:28,745
- They can't hear us.

2333
01:23:28,745 --> 01:23:31,375
Maybe if we get closer
to where they're working.

2334
01:23:31,375 --> 01:23:32,215
- Smart.

2335
01:23:32,215 --> 01:23:33,892
- Gee, we got one deer leg.

2336
01:23:33,892 --> 01:23:35,260
We're going to use it everywhere.

2337
01:23:35,260 --> 01:23:37,560
- [Both] Help! Help!

2338
01:23:37,560 --> 01:23:39,195
- [Mike] We're down here!

2339
01:23:39,195 --> 01:23:41,127
- You have to be heard,
understood, and pleasing.

2340
01:23:41,127 --> 01:23:44,127
Use plenty of lip and tongue action.

2341
01:23:45,819 --> 01:23:46,652
- Help.

2342
01:23:47,496 --> 01:23:48,329
- Louder.

2343
01:23:48,329 --> 01:23:49,971
- Help, we're down here.

2344
01:23:49,971 --> 01:23:52,165
(calling for help in distance)

2345
01:23:52,165 --> 01:23:53,868
- Chad, I hear someone.

2346
01:23:53,868 --> 01:23:55,536
- Calvin Klein Jeans.

2347
01:23:55,536 --> 01:23:58,456
- Mike, Carol, we hear you!

2348
01:23:58,456 --> 01:24:00,112
- But we don't care!

2349
01:24:00,112 --> 01:24:00,945
- It's Kingman.

2350
01:24:00,945 --> 01:24:01,952
They heard us!

2351
01:24:01,952 --> 01:24:04,666
(screeching)
- I hear you too.

2352
01:24:04,666 --> 01:24:07,686
(screaming, chuckling)
- If it's not one thing,

2353
01:24:07,686 --> 01:24:09,258
it's another in this crazy cave.

2354
01:24:09,258 --> 01:24:10,091
Whew.

2355
01:24:12,258 --> 01:24:13,408
- Oh look, I got a walleye,

2356
01:24:13,408 --> 01:24:14,479
a couple of northerns.

2357
01:24:14,479 --> 01:24:16,146
No big lunkers here.

2358
01:24:17,364 --> 01:24:19,459
- And this is the power
line foreman, Kingman.

2359
01:24:19,459 --> 01:24:20,919
He's going to help us
